    id: 'r04', lv: 1, title: "The FoldBot 3000",
    text: "Jada had a serious problem, and its name was laundry. Every Sunday, her mother made her fold a huge mountain of clean clothes. And every Sunday, Jada grumbled that there had to be a more efficient method.\n\nSo she invented one. She used an old remote-control car, two kitchen spatulas, and an alarming amount of tape. She named her robot the FoldBot 3000, even though there had never been a FoldBot 1, 2, or 2,999.\n\nOn Sunday morning, Jada set the FoldBot beside the laundry basket and pressed the big red button. The machine whirred to life. Its spatula arms flapped, seized a T-shirt, and folded it into a flawless square.\n\n'It works!' Jada shouted triumphantly.\n\nThen it folded a sock, and then a towel. Then it folded the newspaper that Dad was reading, right out of his hands.\n\n'Jada,' Dad said slowly.\n\nThe FoldBot rolled across the living room, folding a pillowcase, a dish towel, and the corner of the rug. Then it turned toward Pickles, the cat, who was napping peacefully in a warm patch of sunlight.\n\nJada dove across the carpet and slammed the red button just in time. Pickles opened one eye, yawned, and went back to sleep, apparently unaware of her narrow escape.\n\nMom silently surveyed the neat stack of shirts, the crumpled newspaper, the folded rug, and finally her daughter.\n\n'Version two,' Jada announced quickly, before anyone else could say a word, 'will have a stop button that works from across the room.'",
